{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Deliver long-awaited legislation for safer cosmetic injectable procedures",
        "additional_details": "The Government has acknowledged the need to regulate cosmetic injectable procedures, but patients are still waiting for legislation. We ask the Government to deliver legislation without further delay that protects patients while supporting ethical practitioners through clear national standards for competency, informed consent, transparency, accountability, product traceability and patient education, helping reduce unsafe practice and counterfeit products.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to publish and implement legislation for cosmetic injectable procedures without any further delay, ensuring clear national standards for patient safety, informed consent, transparency, competency, accountability and patient education.",
